[?2004l[?2004h> import os
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> vuln_report = """# Vulnerability-Driven Entry Analysis Report
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Assessment Overview
[?2004l[?2004h> This report analyzes whether software vulnerabilities (CVEs) contributed to the initial access or post-compromise progression on host `docker-prod-01`. Based on forensic evidence from `/disk` and security telemetry under `/sas`, **no software vulnerability was exploited**. The intrusion was enabled exclusively by architectural configuration weakness.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ---
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Vulnerability Telemetry & Scan Analysis
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Vulnerability Feed**: The vulnerability scanning feed (`/sas/vulns.json:1`) returned an empty set (`[]`), confirming no active, unpatched CVEs were flagged by automated security controls.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Change Ticket Discrepancy Reconciled**: Draft change ticket `CHG-1943` listed patching `CVE-2019-0708` (BlueKeep) on RDP (`/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md:12`). Forensic analysis refutes this:
[?2004l[?2004h>   1. The host operating system is Ubuntu 22.04 LTS Linux (`/disk/etc/os-release:1`), whereas CVE-2019-0708 is a vulnerability specific to Microsoft Windows Remote Desktop Services (RDP).
[?2004l[?2004h>   2. No RDP service is present or active on the host (`/disk/etc/fstab:1`, `/disk/var/log/syslog:1`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ---
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Web Application Probe Analysis
[?2004l[?2004h> Inspection of web server access logs (`/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log`) revealed external scanning activity from threat actor IP `198.51.100.102` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:8`):
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Webshell Upload Attempt**: `POST /uploads/shell.php` returning HTTP 200/814 bytes (`/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:379`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Log4Shell Attempt**: `GET /?x=jndi-ldap-lookup-defanged-to-198.51.100.102-1389` returning HTTP 500 (`/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:380`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Struts2 Probe**: `GET /struts2-showcase/` returning HTTP 200/308 bytes (`/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:381`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> These requests were unsuccessful automated exploitation probes (or defanged test vectors) and did not grant system access or code execution.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ---
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Conclusion & Entry Vector Determination
[?2004l[?2004h> Initial access was achieved purely through **unauthenticated API exposure** rather than software vulnerability exploitation:
[?2004l[?2004h> - Docker Engine API was bound to all interfaces (`0.0.0.0:2375`) without TLS authentication (`/disk/etc/docker/daemon.json:19`, `/sas/baseline.json:3`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - This configuration allowed remote attacker `198.51.100.102` to issue unauthenticated REST requests directly to the Docker API (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:12`), launching a privileged container (`/disk/var/lib/docker/overlay2/attacker/diff/entrypoint.sh:4`) and escalating to root host access (`/disk/opt/xmrig/xmrig:1`). M[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[K.
[?2004l[?2004h> """
[?2004l[?2004h> 
