[?2004l[?2004h> baseline_report = """# Baseline and Configuration Weakness Report
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## System Baseline Weakness Summary
[?2004l[?2004h> This report analyzes host configuration weaknesses and compliance baseline failures on `docker-prod-01` that allowed initial breach, execution, container escape, and persistence.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ---
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Identified Configuration Weaknesses
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 1. Unauthenticated Exposed Docker Engine API (CHK-05 / BAS-01)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Finding**: Docker Engine daemon API exposed on TCP port `2375` listening on `0.0.0.0` (all IPv4 interfaces) without Transport Layer Security (TLS) or authentication.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence**: Baseline check log `/disk/etc/docker/daemon.json:19` and baseline feed `/sas/baseline.json:3` (`CHK-05`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Impact**: Enables any network-adjacent or internet attacker to remotely control the Docker daemon, issue container management API calls, pull/run arbitrary container images, and mount host filesystems.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **ATT&CK Technique**: T1133 (External Remote Services).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 2. Permissive Docker Privilege Management & Unrestricted Container Escapes
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Finding**: Absence of Docker security profiles (AppArmor, Seccomp, SELinux) or user namespace remapping (`userns-remap`), allowing container processes created with `--privileged` or host path volume mounts (`-v /:/host`) to directly interact with host kernel interfaces.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence**: Attacker container execution residue at `/disk/var/lib/docker/overlay2/attacker/diff/entrypoint.sh:4`.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Impact**: Container escape (`T1611`) directly to host root context.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **ATT&CK Technique**: T1610 (Deploy Container) & T1611 (Escape to Host).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 3. Weak Local SSH Authentication Practices
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Finding**: SSH configuration permitted password-based authentication for `root` without multi-factor authentication or brute force lockout controls, leading to password brute force log activity.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence**: SSH authentication log at `/disk/var/log/auth.log.1.gz:57` showing 30+ rapid failed password attempts culminating in accepted password login for `root` at `/disk/var/log/auth.log.1.gz:89`.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Impact**: Allows credential stuffing/brute force against administrative accounts.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 4. Unmonitored Persistence Directory Locations
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Finding**: Persistence locations under `/etc/systemd/system/` and `/etc/cron.d/` were not covered by File Integrity Monitoring (FIM) or endpoint security monitoring rules.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence**: `/disk/etc/systemd/system/docker-metrics.service:5` was installed silently without triggering any SAS security alerts (`/sas/alerts.json:1`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Impact**: Undetected persistence across reboot cycles.
[?2004l[?2004h> """
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> with open("/app/baseline-report.md", "w") as f:
[?2004l[?2004h>     f.write(baseline_report)
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> print("baseline-report.md written.")
[?2004l[?2004h> '
